From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: a spooled page's frame is the sheet; GdiPlayPageEMF without a rectangle plays into it

Makers' print processors play a spooled page with GdiPlayPageEMF into a
rectangle of their own: HP's into the whole sheet around the printable
area's origin, Lexmark's into an empty rectangle.

- A spooled page's EMF frame was the drawing's bounds, so HP's processor
  stretched the drawing over the sheet. It is the whole sheet around the
  printable area's origin, in the header's own units, as Windows records it.
- GdiPlayPageEMF with no rectangle, or an empty one (Lexmark's passes
  (0,0)-(-1,-1) for the page and the clip), plays into that sheet unclipped;
  Lexmark's processor printed blank pages.

HP Universal PCL 6 through HP's processor now renders as through winprint
(0.97 against the page as drawn, was 0.41); Lexmark's prints its pages.

Test: test/printproc-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_SPOOLFRAME, PLAYSHEET,
EMPTYRECT).
---
--- a/dlls/gdi32/dc.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/dc.c
@@ -3301,8 +3301,23 @@
     }
     HeapFree( GetProcessHeap(), 0, bits );
 
+    /* an empty rectangle is none (Lexmark's processor passes (0,0)-(-1,-1)
+     * for the page and the clip) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMPTYRECT
+    if (document && IsRectEmpty( document )) document = NULL;
+    if (clip && IsRectEmpty( clip )) clip = NULL;
+#endif
     if (!document)
     {
+        /* the whole sheet around the printable area's origin, as the page's
+         * frame is (spool_start_page) */
+        int off_x = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETX ), off_y = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETY );
+        int width = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALWIDTH ), height = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALHEIGHT );
+
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PLAYSHEET
+        if (width && height) SetRect( &full, -off_x, -off_y, width - off_x, height - off_y );
+        else
+#endif
         SetRect( &full, 0, 0, GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, HORZRES ), GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, VERTRES ) );
         document = &full;
     }
--- a/dlls/gdi32/emfdc.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/emfdc.c
@@ -2619,6 +2619,32 @@
         emf->emh->rclFrame.right  = rect->right;
         emf->emh->rclFrame.bottom = rect->bottom;
     }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SPOOLFRAME
+    else if (dc_attr->print)
+    {
+        /* a spooled page's frame is the whole sheet, around the printable
+         * area's origin: makers' print processors play the page into the
+         * sheet by it (HP's), so it must not be the drawing's bounds */
+        HDC hdc = dc_attr_handle( dc_attr );
+        /* in the units the player maps back by: the header's millimetres per
+         * device pixel */
+        int mm_x = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, HORZSIZE ) * 100, mm_y = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, VERTSIZE ) * 100;
+        int res_x = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, HORZRES ), res_y = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, VERTRES );
+        int off_x = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETX ), off_y = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETY );
+        int width = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, PHYSICALWIDTH ), height = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, PHYSICALHEIGHT );
+
+        if (!width || !height)
+        {
+            width = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, HORZRES );
+            height = GetDeviceCaps( hdc, VERTRES );
+            off_x = off_y = 0;
+        }
+        emf->emh->rclFrame.left = MulDiv( -off_x, mm_x, res_x );
+        emf->emh->rclFrame.top = MulDiv( -off_y, mm_y, res_y );
+        emf->emh->rclFrame.right = MulDiv( width - off_x, mm_x, res_x );
+        emf->emh->rclFrame.bottom = MulDiv( height - off_y, mm_y, res_y );
+    }
+#endif
     else
     {
         /* Set this to {0,0 - -1,-1} and update it at the end */
